    id: 'anomaly-Meteor-Impact-Craters-81',
    parentId: 'craters-br',
    name: 'Granby Crater',
    description: 'Granby is an impact crater in Östergötland, Sweden, located to the southeast of Vadstena. It is estimated to have formed about 470 million years ago (Middle Ordovician). The crater is 3 kilometres (1.9 mi) in diameter and is not exposed at the surface.\n\nAlternative Lore: Alternative researchers note that the Granby crater site aligns with major planetary grid lines, suggesting it acted as a geological focal point. Dowsers and electromagnetic surveyors report intense magnetic anomalies and local gravitational fluctuations near the rim, leading to claims of a permanent telluric vortex at 58.4167, 14.9333.',
