    parentId: 'craters-br',
    name: 'Karikkoselkä',
    description: 'Karikkoselkä is a lake formed in an impact crater in Petäjävesi, Finland. Karikkoselkä is located in Central Finland approximately 30 km east from the centre of Keurusselkä, a much older and larger impact crater. Most lakes in the region are elongated in northwest–southeast direction due to glaciation, but Karikkoselkä is strikingly round. Many shatter cones, rock formations that form under the extreme pressures of impact, have been found around the lake. Further evidence comes from aeromagnetic maps, which show a clear magnetic anomaly in the impact crater area. In addition, samples collected...\n\nAlternative Lore: Ufologists and fringe researchers speculate that Karikkoselkä may hide a deep, covert subterranean facility or D.U.M.B. nested within the impact-compacted bedrock. The natural geological shielding is thought to provide perfect cover for advanced aerospace tests and electromagnetic defense arrays shielded from external satellite scan telemetry.',
