    name: 'Siljan',
    description: 'Siljan, in Dalarna in central Sweden, is Sweden\'s seventh largest lake. The cumulative area of Siljan and the adjacent, smaller lakes Orsasjön and Insjön is 354 km2 (137 sq mi). Siljan reaches a maximum depth of 134 m (440 ft), and its surface is situated 161 m (528 ft) above sea level. This renders the lowest point of the basin at 27 metres (89 ft) above sea level. The largest town on its shore is Mora.\n\nAlternative Lore: Some alternative theorists suggest the Siljan (lake) event was not a meteoric strike, but the crash site of a massive extraterrestrial vehicle or ancient city-ship. Rumors claim that deep core geological drilling at this location secretly aims to map and retrieve hyper-dense alloy hull components buried beneath the crystalline melt sheets.',
