    description: 'Obolon\' crater (Ukrainian: Оболонь) is a 20 km (12 mi) diameter buried meteorite impact crater situated near the village of Obolon, about 200 km (120 mi) southeast of Kyiv in Poltava Oblast, Ukraine. The site has been drilled, which revealed the presence of shocked minerals and impact melt rock; the high chlorine content of the latter suggesting that the area was covered by shallow sea at the time of impact. One estimate puts the age at 169 ± 7 million years (Middle Jurassic).\n\nAlternative Lore: This location is cited by catastrophe theorists as a major contributor to a historical global civilization reset. The massive kinetic energy released at Obolon\' crater is hypothesized to have triggered widespread seismic upheaval, soot clouds, and massive tsunamis, leaving deep scars in local mythology of fire falling from the heavens.',
