    parentId: 'craters-br',
    name: 'Roter Kamm Crater',
    description: 'Roter Kamm (German: Red Ridge) is a meteorite crater, located in the Sperrgebiet, within the Namibian section of the Namib Desert, approximately 80 kilometres (50 mi) north of Oranjemund and 12 kilometres (7.5 mi) southwest of Aurus Mountain in the ǁKaras Region. The crater is 2.5 kilometres (1.6 mi) in diameter and is 130 metres (430 ft) deep. The age is estimated at 4.81 ± 0.5 Ma, placing it in the Pliocene. The crater is exposed at the surface, but its original floor is covered by sand deposits at least 100 metres (330 ft) thick.\n\nAlternative Lore: According to alternative history theorists, Roter Kamm crater represents a ground-zero site of an ancient high-yield thermonuclear blast or particle-beam weapon strike predating recorded history. Proponents point to the extreme presence of shocked quartz and glass-like tektites as evidence of localized artificial vitrification rather than a natural kinetic impact.',
